BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:c930ac473c9c7380@zcyber-gtm.local
DTSTAMP:20260727T160011Z
DTSTART:20260723T170000Z
DTEND:20260723T220000Z
SUMMARY:Chicago InfoSec Managers Workshop - Western Burbs (Lisle)
DESCRIPTION:<h1>​Leading Under Pressure</h1><h2>​How Stress\, Communication &amp\; Leadership Behaviors Shape Cybersecurity Team Performance</h2><p>​Cybersecurity leaders are expected to operate in high-pressure environments where constant escalation\, incident fatigue\, staffing strain\, and nonstop communication demands have become normalized.</p><p>​But stress does not stay isolated to individuals.<br>It spreads through teams.</p><p>​The way leaders communicate during pressure — especially after incidents\, mistakes\, or prolonged overload — directly shapes psychological safety\, team trust\, engagement\, and long-term performance.</p><p>​Leading Under Pressure is a highly interactive 4-hour workshop designed specifically for cybersecurity managers and team leaders who want to better understand:</p><ul><li><p>​how stress changes leadership behavior</p></li><li><p>​how communication impacts team performance</p></li><li><p>​how burnout silently propagates through organizations</p></li><li><p>​how to build healthier\, more sustainable cybersecurity teams</p></li></ul><p>​This is not traditional leadership training.<br>It is a practical\, psychologically intelligent operational leadership workshop grounded in the real-world realities of cybersecurity.</p><p>​Participants will experience:</p><ul><li><p>​realistic cybersecurity leadership scenarios</p></li><li><p>​a proprietary leadership style assessment</p></li><li><p>​communication-under-pressure exercises</p></li><li><p>​burnout &amp\; stress awareness frameworks</p></li><li><p>​practical recovery and sustainable performance strategies</p></li><li><p>​facilitated peer discussion with other cybersecurity leaders</p></li></ul><p>​Pilot workshops are intentionally limited to a small cohort of participants to encourage meaningful discussion\, reflection\, and feedback that will help shape future Green Shoe Consulting workshops and the GROE learning platform.</p><p>​Ideal for:<br>Cybersecurity managers\, SOC leaders\, IR managers\, security engineering managers\, and team leads responsible for both operational performance and people leadership.</p><p>​4 CPE / CEU eligible hours.</p><p>​Cost: $350 per attendee</p> | Source: Chicago InfoSec Events Calendar | Tags: cyber\, cybersecurity\, health\, infosec\, security | https://calendar.google.com/calendar/ical/ChicagoInfoSecEvents@gmail.com/public/basic.ics
LOCATION:4225 Naperville Rd\, Lisle\, IL
URL:https://calendar.google.com/calendar/ical/ChicagoInfoSecEvents@gmail.com/public/basic.ics
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
