UID:7cd6641fab732aed@zcyber-gtm.local
DTSTAMP:20260727T160011Z
DTSTART:20260729T120000Z
DTEND:20260729T133000Z
SUMMARY:(CS)²AI Online™: Security Lifecycles of Connected Power Infrastructure
DESCRIPTION:Nashville Cyber Security for Control Systems [https://events.zoom.us/ev/Akgd1vdEBM3_-dVIIC984km2rdNba4A7BSm8oQ3Acj8AMaAqEuiG~AgGQltEj_HyS7hzBVFo65QjDQHd2E-V1ve9fe5tBu5wSeD96KYTH_bDG5GJkbKM7mTSe4ZhY8-zItF2ZDowp-8QxwA](https://events.zoom.us/ev/Akgd1vdEBM3_-dVIIC984km2rdNba4A7BSm8oQ3Acj8AMaAqEuiG~AgGQltEj_HyS7hzBVFo65QjDQHd2E-V1ve9fe5tBu5wSeD96KYTH_bDG5GJkbKM7mTSe4ZhY8-zItF2ZDowp-8QxwA) The power industry has largely solved the question of whether critical power assets should be connected. UPS systems\, PDUs\, and power management platforms are now routinely integrated with cloud services\, remote support\, and operational analytics. The harder question is whether these assets are deployed in a way that justifies the trust being placed in them. Even when products are Secure by Design and Secure by Default\, commissioning and integration decisions often determine the real cybersecurity outcome. Yet these activities are frequently led by teams focused on operational performance and uptime rather than cyber risk. This session examines why commissioning may be the most important security event in a power asset's lifecycle and outlines practical approaches for establishing security from day one through secure commissioning\, secure-by-deployment principles\, and lifecycle risk management. Join our ICS/OT Cybersecurity star Mike Holcomb and Power specialist Saltanat Mashirova for this in-depth talk\, and be sure to bring your questions for her! [https://events.zoom.us/ev/Akgd1vdEBM3_-dVIIC984km2rdNba4A7BSm8oQ3Acj8AMaAqEuiG~AgGQltEj_HyS7hzBVFo65QjDQHd2E-V1ve9fe5tBu5wSeD96KYTH_bDG5GJkbKM7mTSe4ZhY8-zItF2ZDowp-8QxwA](https://events.zoom.us/ev/Akgd1vdEBM3_-dVIIC984km2rdNba4A7BSm8oQ3Acj8AMaAqEuiG~AgGQltEj_HyS7hzBVFo65QjDQHd2E-V1ve9fe5tBu5wSeD96KYTH_bDG5GJkbKM7mTSe4ZhY8-zItF2ZDowp-8QxwA) \\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Becoming a paid member is quick and easy (and helps us keep offering free educational opportunities!). Please join now! [https://www.cs2ai.org/plans-pricing](https://www.cs2ai.org/plans-pricing) All past seminars and symposiums are available to paid [CS2AI.ORG](https://www.cs2ai.org/) members. Check out the Resources area of our website in the Members Portal [https://www.cs2ai.org/](https://www.cs2ai.org/) Certificates for Professional Development/Continuing Education Units (PDUs/CEUs) are available for all registered individuals who attend at least one hour of the event. [https://www.cs2ai.org/get-involved](https://www.cs2ai.org/get-involved) \\*Please note that (CS)²AI Online™ events are provided free of charge as educational career development content through the support of our paid members and the generous contributions of our corporate Strategic Alliance Partners. Contact information used in registering for our directly supported seminars may be shared with sponsors funding those specific events. Unless noted on our Zoom Event registration page\, all events are open for direct funding support. © Control System Cyber Security Association International 2026 | Source: Nashville Cyber Security for Control Systems | Tags: cyber\, cybersecurity\, risk\, security | https://www.meetup.com/nashville-cyber-security-for-control-systems/events/315789329/
LOCATION:
URL:https://www.meetup.com/nashville-cyber-security-for-control-systems/events/315789329/
END:VEVENT
