SUMMARY:Analog Electronics for Guitar Pedals
DESCRIPTION:Noisebridge Hackerspace **Learn about the LM386\, amp on a chip** — Pedal Building Workshop The LM386 is a tiny power amp chip used to build small amps\, and distortion pedals. We will breadboard a 1/2 watt amp or the Smash Drive\, an overdrive distortion circuit. No experience needed. Beginners welcome! Free and open to all\, as always. Come make some noise. 📍 Noisebridge\, 272 Capp St\, San Francisco | Source: DC415 San Francisco | Tags: security | https://www.meetup.com/noisebridge/events/315785319/
